{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Low_level.Fp_licence</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"arrayjit","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Ir","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Low_level","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Fp_licence","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>The licences of the rounding-changing algebra over the reals (gh-ocannl-998), one field per licence, each true when that family of rewrites may run:</p><ul><li><code>contract</code>: fusing a floating <code>a * b + c</code> into one <code>FMA</code> (one rounding instead of two);</li><li><code>reassociate</code>: constant reassociation through <code>Add</code>/<code>Mul</code>, re-parenthesized subtraction chains, the multiplication/division interchanges, and unrolling known integer powers into multiplications;</li><li><code>finite_math</code>: the zero identities <code>x + 0 = x</code>, <code>0 - x = -x</code> and <code>0 * x = 0</code>, which hold only for finite operands and ignoring the sign of zero.</li></ul><p>Integer precisions take every licence but the floating-only arms (the interchanges and contraction): reassociation is exact in wrapping arithmetic, and the index canonicalizer relies on it.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> t</span><span> = </span><span>{</span></code><ol><li id=\"type-t.contract\" class=\"def record field anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.contract\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>contract : <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.bool;</span></code></li><li id=\"type-t.reassociate\" class=\"def record field anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.reassociate\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>reassociate : <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.bool;</span></code></li><li id=\"type-t.finite_math\" class=\"def record field anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.finite_math\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>finite_math : <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.bool;</span></code></li></ol><code><span>}</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-include\"><details open=\"open\"><summary class=\"spec include\"><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Sexplib0</span>.Sexpable.S <span class=\"keyword\">with</span> <span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">t</span> := <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">t</span></span></span></code></summary><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-t_of_sexp\"><a href=\"#val-t_of_sexp\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> t_of_sexp : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Sexplib0__</span>.Sexp.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <a href=\"#type-t\">t</a></span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-sexp_of_t\"><a href=\"#val-sexp_of_t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> sexp_of_t : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Sexplib0__</span>.Sexp.t</span></code></div></div></details></div><div class=\"odoc-include\"><details open=\"open\"><summary class=\"spec include\"><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Ppx_compare_lib</span>.Equal.S <span class=\"keyword\">with</span> <span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">t</span> := <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">t</span></span></span></code></summary><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-equal\"><a href=\"#val-equal\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> equal : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\